	(text "The oscillator should be tuned to\n(crystal filter center frequency) - 700 Hz\nExample: \nFilter CF = 8.998.280 Hz\nOsc. Freq = 8.997.580 Hz\nThe expected output power to 50 Ohms is about\n4 dBm on the main frequency (probably, mismatched).\n\nSome experimentation may be required.\nTry different coils and crystals if the oscillator\ndoesn’t tune to the required frequency.\nLow Q crystals are preferable in this circuit."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16.51 166.37 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "078eec4b-0941-40ac-a66e-2d73ca55bb0c")
	)
	(text "This feedback amplifier gives 10..12 dB of gain\nat 9 Mhz depending on the specific transistor."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 134.62 163.83 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "224d858a-a608-4c8b-b88e-0a10a5d35d1c")
	)
	(text "8 dB attenuator. Change if necessary.\nThe goal is to get about 6-8 dBm after\namplifying and filtering the signal."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 87.63 144.78 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "711dc703-f3dd-4209-94e9-00cca19225b7")
	)
	(text "The secret of a superheterodyne receiver free of spurious \nsignals is a clean BFO. The signal of Si5351 is way too dirty\nand can’t be used as a BFO. Trust me, I’ve tried many times.\n\nFor this project I wanted a clean, well-matched to 50 Ohm,\n7 dBm BFO. However, if space is limited, try removing\nthe attenuator and the amplifier, and then - the filter.\nChances are everything will work adequately without them."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 33.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b3b5ce8f-4824-4cd7-9680-8d59532cc861")
	)
	(text "About 7 dBm pure sine wave\nwell-matched to 50 Ohms."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 255.27 88.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "bdf30cf3-15af-4b40-a6c2-4c7fc4d59e1a")
	)
	(text "9 MHz LPF, 0.1 dB ripple Chebyshev type.\n1.14u = 16T @ T50-6\n1.27u = 17T @ T50-6"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 203.2 130.81 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "c6bee085-d9e6-4c06-88a4-97cc8a0a43b0")
	)
	(text "10T bifilar @ FT37-43"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 149.86 102.87 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ddf567f8-4618-4e7c-973a-94ee7507ae8f")
	)
